# Session Closing Protocol

Do not run full closing rituals for every small edit. Use the smallest evidence
that proves the requested work.

## Normal task closure

- Review your diff.
- Run the most relevant targeted check.
- Report changed files, check result, and any blocker.

## Push/PR/merge/deploy closure

- Run relevant lint/typecheck/test/build.
- Read back GitHub checks and review findings if a PR exists.
- For deploy/release, run the security/deploy gate and health checks.

## Anti-loop rule

If the same check fails twice, stop repeating it. Diagnose a different axis
(source, minimal repro, config, environment, dependency, or documentation), then
make one targeted change.